{"ts":"2026-11-12T15:22:06.519Z","actor":"claude","stage":"factcheck","action":"factcheck.review","details":{"verdict":"pass","notes":"Semantic review: every number traces to a sourced fact (NASA Sun facts: 4.24 light-years, 9.5 trillion km per light-year; NASA Voyager: more than 3 AU per year; Breakthrough Starshot: up to 100 million mph; Lorentz factor: Wikipedia). Derived figures are stated as derived: 89,000 years is 4.24 light-years (about 63,000 AU) at 3 AU a year; 28 years is 4.24 light-years at about 15% of light speed; 223,000 and 10 minutes come from the Lorentz factor at 99.999999999% of light speed. The Starshot page says 'just over 20 years' for a flyby at 20%; we use the 100 million mph speed it states, so the time is 28 years, and say so. The clock slows for the crew relative to Earth, which is the point of the episode. Nothing is claimed about visibility or direction."},"gitSha":"bfff8f1"}
