{"ts":"2026-11-12T17:12:24.742Z","actor":"claude","stage":"factcheck","action":"factcheck.review","details":{"verdict":"pass","notes":"Re-review after correcting the Voyager figure. Old fact voyager-speed was wrong (stated 4.24 ly ≈ 63,000 AU; it is ≈268,000 AU) and its wording ran backwards ('more than 3 AU/yr' → 'over 89,000 years'). New sourced fact voyager1-speed-nasa: NASA gives 17.0 km/s; 4.24 × 9.461e12 km ÷ 17.0 km/s ≈ 74,800 yr → 'about seventy-five thousand years' (hook, voyager card, compare bar, post). Hook 'Seventy-five thousand years… Voyager 1 would need to reach the nearest star, Proxima Centauri, 4.24 light-years away' matches proxima-distance. Compare is now linear and labelled 'Drawn to scale'; 28 vs 75,000 renders Starshot as a sliver, and 'barely a sliver' is literally true (0.04%). Starshot 15%/28 years, Lorentz 223,000 / 10 min (4.24 yr ÷ 223,000 ≈ 10 min) and Voyager 1 one light-day (NASA: 18 Nov 2026) unchanged and re-verified. Post copy updated to the 17 km/s / 75,000 years figures and the Voyager 1 page."},"gitSha":"56e31e5"}
